 "missing_frames": [],
 "arc": "V-step: out-out, in-in on a four-count, traced slightly slowed so each landing reads. Frames 0-3 step the character-left foot out and away from centre, arms folding up to chest height with the elbows bent, torso staying upright and the shoulders bouncing on the count. Frames 4-7 send the character-right foot out to the opposite corner — the widest point of the V — with the weight rolling to the ball of the standing foot and the opposite hip cocking on each landing.\n\nFrames 8-15 close the V back in: the character-right foot comes home, arms drop low past the hips as the body sinks, then the character-left closes and the arms tuck back inside the shoulders. The loop closes with both feet down at the narrow point, which is where frame 0 picks up. Keep the bounce driven from the knees and the arms small — this move is footwork, the upper body just rides it.",
